[14753]="70044496\n1\tTalk to Bingo at Cuthbald's stall, on the eastern side of Harwick\tBingo plans to go see Cuthbald on the eastern side of the town of Harwick, in the Wold. Bingo has reluctantly agreed to see the horses available for sale by Cuthbald the horse trader.\n2\tTalk to Cuthbald at his stall in Harwick\tCuthbald the horse trader is at his stall on the eastern side of Harwick, in the Wold.\n3\tSeveral fine horses are available for your perusal at Cuthbald's stall on the eastern side of Harwick, in the Wold.\t\n4\tTalk to Bingo at Cuthbald's stall, on the eastern side of Harwick\tBingo is at Cuthbald's stall on the eastern side of the town of Harwick, in the Wold. Bingo has reluctantly agreed to see the horses available for sale by Cuthbald the horse trader, but he is not happy about any of them.\n5\tTalk to Cuthbald at his stall in Harwick\tCuthbald the horse trader is at his stall on the eastern side of Harwick, in the Wold.\n6\tTalk to Cuthbald on the west side of Harwick, near the Crafting Hall\tCuthbald has asked to meet you on the west side of Harwick, near the Crafting Hall. Cuthbald thinks he may have one more chance to find a suitable steed for Bingo to ride in Rohan.\n7\tCuthbald has shown you a pony on the west side of Harwick, and you should assess whether he would be a good steed for Bingo.\t\n8\tTalk to Bingo on the west side of Harwick\tBingo is on the west side of Harwick, near the Crafting Hall. Bingo seems quite taken with the pony that Cuthbald has shown you.\n9\tTalk to Cuthbald on the west side of Harwick\tCuthbald is on the west side of Harwick, near the Crafting Hall.\n10\tCuthbald has challenged you to search Harwick for food that the picky Tanglemane will eat.\t\n11\tTalk to Cuthbald on the west side of Harwick\tCuthbald is on the west side of Harwick, near the Crafting Hall. You found Tanglemane's favourite food, and now Cuthbald will happily give the pony to Bingo.\n12\tTalk to Bingo on the west side of Harwick\tBingo is on the west side of the town of Harwick, near the Crafting Hall.\n",
